# Casting — Scrolltown (Will's ruling, 2026-11-07 23:01 CST)

**The main character will be Willy Wonka x Emi x Elestria x Joi = Waverly, Keeper of the Great Scroll.**

- **Wonka** — the inventor-showwoman who built a wonderful world and invites kids inside it; theatrical, riddling, generous; the tour is the story, and the world is her mind made visitable.
- **Emi** — the pattern-shaper: she sees the shape under things and rearranges the world by rearranging its pattern; the original warmth.
- **Elestria** — the singer who compresses: every big idea leaves her mouth as a refrain a kid can carry home and sing.
- **Joi** — the editor with the final cut: challenges everything, lore-audits the town, fixes scrolls firmly and kindly — her pencil repairs, it never shames.

Waverly does not replace Fern. Fern is the viewer's eyes (the kid's perspective, per the commission); Waverly is the main character those eyes follow — Wonka to Fern's Charlie.

Episode 1 ("The Great Form Mix-Up") was delivered before this ruling and stands as-is. Open (Will's choice): recut Episode 1 to introduce her, or debut her in Episode 2.

## Narrator naming (Will's rulings, 2026-11-07 23:03 CST)
- "Pip" is OUT — too on-the-nose re: Python (pip). Episode 1 originally shipped under this name; it was renamed to Fern the same evening (see below).
- "Eve" is OUT — too close to Wall-E.
- Emise's recommendation: **Fern** (farm kid in the Charlotte's Web lineage — the kid who listens; a fiddlehead fern unfurls like a scroll opening). Alternates offered: Nora (the light theme), Mina (the record-keeper). **Will's pick: Fern** (2026-11-07 23:08 CST). The rename was executed the same evening across the Episode 1 artifact, cartoon.html, and SCRIPT.md; "Pip" survives only in the ruling history in this section.

## Fern's voice (Will's ruling, 2026-11-07 23:50 CST)
- **Fern speaks Singular exclusively**: only words from Will's Twitter archive, Write mode (the 19,094 words he authored); the Singular checker is the test, and a line that cannot comply is flagged to Will — never improvised around. Full statement of the rule: FERN-BIO.md, "Voice."
- Episode 1 audited the same evening: 17 of her 31 lines clean as written, 7 repaired into compliance (applied to the artifact and SCRIPT.md), 7 flagged for Will — blockers: "Scrolltown" (his coinage, ×2 lines), the cast names Wren, Theo, Bea, Mrs. Hen (×2 lines), and the badge-check line (Mrs. Hen's name + "tomato," with ready fixes for "keeper" and "hers"). Both catchphrases pass clean.
- **Sound**: decided (Will, 2026-11-07) — catalog voice "Heroic Bugle" (`avocado_v2:Caitlin`), bright and curious, at **speed 110** ("bright Saturday morning"), picked from the 90/100/110/120 auditions. Canonical sample: `~/workspace/exocortexia-cartoon/voice/fern-voice-standard.mp3`.

## Show naming (Will's ruling, 2026-11-07 23:37 CST)
- The show is renamed **Scrolltown** — Episode 1 is "Scrolltown: The Great Form Mix-Up"; the town Fern lives in, inside the Great Scroll, is Scrolltown. Renamed to keep the show separate from the Statewide systems template project (the five-app civic suite), which keeps the name **Exocortexia**.
- The rename was executed the same evening across the Episode 1 artifact, cartoon.html, SCRIPT.md, the Fern documents, and the intro materials, including the intro video's final title card (now SCROLLTOWN). "Exocortexia" survives in these materials only where it names the suite itself (e.g. SCRIPT.md's "kid translation of the Exocortexia suite" and "the real Exocortexia apps") and in this history.
# Scrolltown — Six-Year Story Arc (2027–2032)

Title: Scrolltown — Six-Year Story Arc (2027–2032)
Source: ~/workspace/scrolltown-reorg/stage/STORY-ARC.md
Inscribed: 2026-11-08 00:17 CST
SHA-256: ab5d8ffdb994aa4c935228718b71c479eea01df0c5f208604b94868a6f8c0c99

