4. Cutaway stack-diagram slide (build once, reuse in the cutdown).
5. End card.

**Confirm during recording (not asserted as fact anywhere above)**

- Which phext the site offers a signed-out visitor (demo/welcome
  content, its name, and whether browsing it needs sign-in today).
- Exact on-screen labels/gestures for: opening a phext, the dimension
  navigation UI, coordinate jump, search box, save. (Capabilities are
  verified from the phext-lattice repo — Navigator/search/overlay-save
  are real — but the hosted UI's exact presentation is checked on the
  day, and B-roll follows the checker, not this script.)
- Whether the hosted editor offers a visitor a download/export of
  the phext being browsed. Source check (phext-lattice): the only
  download endpoint in the editor source is the submissions review
  queue — so plan on the fallback in the 5:15 beat (open demo/
  wiki.phext in the plain editor) unless the live site proves
  otherwise on the day.
- Whether a custom phext (e.g. demo/wiki.phext) can be loaded into the
  hosted editor by a visitor, and how (the repo documents /submit as
  a *signed-in* upload-for-review flow — do not present it as a
